menu "Atari 8-bit Bus"

config A8BB_ENABLE_MDNS
    bool "Enable mDNS hostname support"
    default n
    help
        Link mDNS support and advertise a MAC-derived hostname on the local
        network. The boot profile must also enable mDNS at runtime.

config A8BB_CORE0_HOTSPOTS_EXPLICIT_PLACEMENT
    bool "Explicitly place Core0 IRAM hotspots"
    default n
    help
        Put the Core0 hotspot functions together and align iloop_pbi to the
        next 32 KiB boundary. This guarantees separation from the Core1 loop,
        at the cost of additional IRAM address space and reduced heap space.

config A8BB_SIDECAR_ENABLE
    bool "Use the Sidecar coprocessor"
    default n
    help
        Have the host use the Sidecar, an optional second ESP32 coprocessor
        (the app in sidecar/), over the i2slink I2S DMA link. The link and
        protocol live in components/sidecar_link and are always compiled;
        this gates the host code that uses them. The link speed is
        I2SLINK_FRAMES_PER_SECOND in i2slink.h and must match on both ends.
        Incompatible with PROFILE_MODE GPIO or PIN (both need GPIO48); the
        build stops if both are selected. Also turns off the status LED.

endmenu
